# 1Password secret references for local development. References only, never values.
#
# `op run` resolves each op:// reference from 1Password and hands the results to
# docker compose, which passes them into the app container (docker/docker-compose.yml):
#
#     cd docker && op run --env-file=../secrets.env -- docker compose up
#
# This file is committed. op run passes a plain value through unchanged, so a secret
# pasted here would work, and would be committed. Use op:// references only.
#
# Every uncommented reference must resolve, or op run refuses to start. Uncomment a line
# once its item exists, pointing it at your app's vault and item. In the 1Password app,
# a field's menu has "Copy Secret Reference".

# Needed with ->addAuthentication() (OIDC).
# OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=op://guild-starter/oidc/client-secret

# Needed with ->addAuthorization() (Grouper).
# GROUPER_PASSWORD=op://guild-starter/grouper/password

# Needed only when mail goes through a real SMTP server; mailcatcher takes none.
# MAIL_PASSWORD=op://guild-starter/smtp/password

# Read by no code; listed for parity with the deployed environment.
# LDAP_PASSWORD=op://guild-starter/ldap/password
